228e6","position":{"commit_sha":"97b4c69ae21a2441a3885de21d1d0ee6b946c77f","position":"1788408008699496001-d66f80e4-12de-4cbf-90ae-02606eb228e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"84c47780ab18ab3cfe7707ce43e9ea81522d91943acb437bba9ba901e81b502b","event_uuid":"4d476566-d5d4-418f-83b9-ca204e1fb674","position":{"commit_sha":"4f47b340db28bcc0d0a9d5276e3236347880e296","position":"1788408173759968705-4d476566-d5d4-418f-83b9-ca204e1fb674"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"32f1e2064894c0ff86ab8bf79bfce0df909f6b72f8501c0a5de5cf3df1130a4a","event_uuid":"3cb84d9e-bed5-4159-b0d7-1a10362b96f2","position":{"commit_sha":"efa1999dca4cf1058b3584e3db9761b99a6dccb7","position":"1788409798473715001-3cb84d9e-bed5-4159-b0d7-1a10362b96f2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-258_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b49fe82a-1778-4290-aefd-33d2684ae335","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 2557 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2557), from a worktree at current gerrit/main.\n\nReproduced on PRISTINE gerrit/main before changing anything — 1 failed, 5 passed — so this is a main breakage and not something change 2555 introduced. 2555 (F10) is only its first visible victim; every change branched from main inherits it.\n\nAC1: the assertion now reads the VALUE (\"bug\" in _PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES) rather than matching source text.\nAC2: removing \"bug\" from the exemption set in rebar.types turns it RED.\nAC3: re-pointing the gates.py alias — a behaviour-preserving move — keeps it GREEN. That pair is the exact inversion of the old assertion, which went red on the refactor and would have stayed green on a value change.\nAC4: the other five tests in the file are untouched; 7 pass in the file.\n\nOne correction during implementation. My first draft added a second test calling _plan_review_gate_applies to assert a bug is not review-required. That predicate consults gate_enabled, so a bug would read \"not required\" whenever the gate is simply switched OFF — the test would have passed for a reason unrelated to the exemption. Replaced with a config-independent complement assertion: bug exempt while story and task are not, which also stops the first assertion passing by the set growing to cover everything.\n\nGates: make lint and make typecheck clean; 1458 passed / 4 skipped in tests/unit -k \"gates or claim or plan_review\".\n\nNo production behaviour changes — this is a test-only fix.","timestamp":1788408008699496001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-session note from the debug-orchestrator session: I SUBMITTED change 2557 (now MERGED). Flagging clearly because this is your claimed ticket and I did not want the submit to be a surprise.\n\nReasoning: 2557 was already fully gated — LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, submittable true — so nothing was pending on it but the submit itself. Meanwhile main stayed red, and because every change branches from main, EVERY session's CI was inheriting the failure. I hit it independently on change 2556 (ticket 3a02): Verified -1 on a test touching none of that change's three files. I checked out pristine origin/main and reproduced there — 1 failed, 5 passed, identical assertion, and identical on py3.11/3.12/3.13, so deterministic rather than flaky. Your diagnosis and mine match exactly.\n\nLeaving a green main-red fix unsubmitted while three parallel sessions burn CI cycles seemed the worse option. If you had a reason to hold it, say so and I will not do this again — a WIP flag on the change would have stopped me, per CONTRIBUTING §2d.\n\nVerification after the submit: main should now be green on that assertion. I am rebasing 2556 onto it next.","timestamp":1788409798473715001}],"created_at":1788407496556370001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6810994b-ca18-4872-a1ed-67fbc0379b3b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"218e-0ec1-385d-493a"},{"link_uuid":"f7ce23b5-c8d7-4b95-af1d-dfeade8b9586","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"},{"link_uuid":"4d476566-d5d4-418f-83b9-ca204e1fb674","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7266-e7c7-e222-4792"}],"description":"main is RED. tests/unit/test_bug_claim_rca_sequence_docs.py::test_claim_time_exemption_type_registry_includes_bug fails on gerrit/main, and blocks every change branched from it (it is what put change 2555 at Verified -1).\n\n## What happened\n\nA semantic merge conflict between two changes that were each green on their own, which per-patchset CI structurally cannot catch.\n\n- Change 2544 (another session) added the test. It asserts a literal SOURCE STRING: `_PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES = (\"bug\"` must appear in src/rebar/_commands/gates.py.\n- Change 2530 (this epic, mirror F3) consolidated that constant into rebar.types. gates.py:31 now imports it and gates.py:48 reads `_PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES = PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES`.\n\nThe literal is therefore gone (grep count 0 on gerrit/main) while the test asserting it is still present. Confirmed by running it: 1 failed, 5 passed.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe assertion is a CHANGE-DETECTOR: it asserts internal source TEXT rather than observable behavior, so a behavior-preserving consolidation breaks it even though the behavior it cares about — that a bug is claim-time exempt from plan review — is completely unchanged. AGENTS.md is explicit that a test which breaks under a behavior-preserving refactor should be rewritten to assert observable behavior.\n\n## Fix\n\nRewrite the assertion to test the intent directly: that \"bug\" is in the claim-time exemption set as the code actually evaluates it, and that a bug is consequently not review-required. That is strictly STRONGER than the source-text check (it would catch a value change the string match would miss) and it survives refactors. No production behavior changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: the test asserts the exemption VALUE, not source text. Verified by review of the test and by it passing on current main.\n- [ ] AC2: it fails if \"bug\" stops being claim-time exempt. Verified by a mutation removing \"bug\" from the exemption set and seeing RED.\n- [ ] AC3: it survives a behavior-preserving move of the constant. Verified by re-pointing the alias and seeing it stay green.\n- [ ] AC4: the other five tests in the file are untouched and still pass.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_bug_claim_rca_sequence_docs.py -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_bug_claim_rca_sequence_docs.py","reason":"replace the source-text assertion with a behavioral one"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7266-e7c7-e222-4792"],["relates_to","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1ed6414e-285d-4b45-ae6a-5b84bdf697b4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5550-603c-8059-49ab","ticket_type":"bug","title":"main is red: source-text assertion broke on F3 consolidation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1b8513d8-574f-44d4-bb6c-753bbdd312dd","6810994b-ca18-4872-a1ed-67fbc0379b3b","f7ce23b5-c8d7-4b95-af1d-dfeade8b9586","7fffa871-17b8-4513-8f3a-28375034d01b","1ed6414e-285d-4b45-ae6a-5b84bdf697b4","2c7f9f70-7cc2-4ebe-8bf2-37d090885db8","d66f80e4-12de-4cbf-90ae-02606eb228e6","4d476566-d5d4-418f-83b9-ca204e1fb674","3cb84d9e-bed5-4159-b0d7-1a10362b96f2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788409798473715002,"uuid":"b87b4b76-c835-40a7-8e09-22f86b5d2d1c"}